<!--
    The status-bar icon for the app's one notification channel: a torii, the same idea as
    the site's own launcher icon.

    A status-bar icon is alpha-masked and tinted white by the system — only the SHAPE of the
    opaque pixels survives, never the colour. That is why @mipmap/ic_launcher can never be
    used here (it is flat colour on a flat background and would render as a white square)
    and why this is one flat single-colour path with nothing to lose in the mask. It is its
    own file rather than a reuse of the launcher or splash drawable so that an icon tweak on
    either of those can never silently change what the shade shows.

    24dp is the platform's status-bar icon size; the shape is inset from the edges so the
    system's own padding does not clip the posts.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24"
    android:tint="#FFFFFFFF">
    <!-- kasagi (the overhanging top beam), shimaki (the beam under it), two posts. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M2.4,3.6 H21.6 V6.0 H2.4 Z
                          M5.2,7.4 H18.8 V9.4 H5.2 Z
                          M6.4,6.0 H8.8 V20.8 H6.4 Z
                          M15.2,6.0 H17.6 V20.8 H15.2 Z" />
</vector>
